From 23fb1585cbb22fc226883deba91091b878ba13f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegdyd <telegdyd93@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:52:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] jasmine: present queue with latch-based reuse and
 sleeping waits (j0100)

Task 16 build 1, all new behavior off by default.
sweetfb_sleep=1: the CTL_FLUSH, write-wait and timed SwapWait polls sleep
instead of spinning (IODelay), with the same timeouts; slept/spun time in the
SWEET FB and SWEET GPU lines.
sweetfb_queue=1 (needs sweetfb_sleep=1): SwapEnd admits one frame and returns;
a presenter thread flips it once its surfaces finished on the GPU and the
previous flip latched. SwapWait is done only after a later swap latched, so
CoreAnimation draws the next frame into a third surface. A latch that stays
pending is retried and then released by the old timeout, and any protocol fault
switches the boot back to synchronous presentation; the display never halts.
Selector 3 accepts out-of-line BO tables (parameter 9 bit 2) and counts nbo=0
jobs; parameter 9 reports sleep (bit 0) and queue (bit 1). Framebench events
32-36: admit, flip, drop, fallback, guard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
